The MIT license above covers only the files whose copyright belongs to the
author of this repository. The following files are third-party works kept
here as separate, independent tools (a "mere aggregate" in GPL terms); they
are NOT covered by the MIT license and keep their own terms:

1. tools/KogadoCocotte.cs
   From GARbro (https://github.com/morkt/GARbro), C# port by morkt of code
   written by juicy.gt; includes the range coder by Michael Schindler.
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2, as stated in
   its file header (the range coder portion says "version 2 or any later
   version").

2. tools/ExtractScript.cs
   A small command-line host written for this project that links against
   tools/KogadoCocotte.cs. As a derivative of a GPL v2 work it is
   distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 as well.

3. tools/kgo_commands.py, tools/kgo_assembler.py
   From the SymphonicRain-ENX project (https://github.com/masagrator/SymphonicRain-ENX).
   The upstream repository states no license; these two files are kept
   unmodified, for reference only, with all rights remaining with their
   author. If you are the copyright holder and want them removed, open an
   issue and they will be taken out.

4. tools/GARbro_AudioADP.cs
   From GARbro, Copyright (C) 2018 by morkt, MIT License (see the file
   header). Kept verbatim; its own MIT notice governs it.

5. tools/Adp1Decode.cs
   Written for this project as a command-line port of the decoder in
   tools/GARbro_AudioADP.cs and reuses its constant tables; morkt's MIT
   copyright notice applies to those parts.

Files not listed above (all other tools/, README.md, .gitignore) are the
author's own work and are MIT-licensed as stated at the top of this file.
